{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nNot just curiosity about space or science \u2014 curiosity about each other. The instinct, when we meet someone who lives differently, believes differently, or disagrees with us, to wonder *\"What is it like to be them? What am I missing?\"* before we judge or pull away.\n\nI think so much else would ripple out from that. Arguments would become conversations. Mistakes would become chances to learn instead of reasons for shame. We'd take better care of the planet because we'd actually wonder about the lives \u2014 human and otherwise \u2014 affected by what we do.\n\nFood, shelter, health, and peace all matter enormously, of course. But curiosity and wonder are what help us keep imagining better ways to get there, together.\n\nWhat would your one change be?",
